s Haydn edition and its unsatisfactory progress is rather complicated. This matter, which was entrusted to my beloved master, Mandyczewski, always remained a source of great \hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0 
uneasiness to him: he knew better than any one how insufficient the bibliographical preparations had been, and he did not feel young and strong enough to undertake the thorny preparatory work. This was the only reason for the hitch in the publication. The
\hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0  \hich\af0\dbch\af13\loch\f0 position of this unfortunate edition is still the same today: a large part of Haydn\hich\f0 \rquote \loch\f0 
s works is practically unknown to the world, and a complete and reliable list of his works is even yet not obtainable.
